WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.781
Content Security Policy, or CSP, is a browser defense-in-depth control
that can restrict where scripts, styles, images, fonts, frames,
connections, and other resources may load or execute from under browser
rules.

2
00:00:12.781 --> 00:00:19.555
It is especially relevant to XSS risk reduction because it can reduce the
impact of some unsafe rendering mistakes.

3
00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:26.330
CSP works best when the application already separates code from data and
has predictable frontend asset behavior.

4
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.219
Source concepts define which locations are allowed for different resource
types.

5
00:00:31.219 --> 00:00:38.273
Nonce and hash concepts can support specific approved inline resources
without allowing every inline script or style.

6
00:00:38.273 --> 00:00:45.816
Reducing unsafe inline behavior makes CSP easier to maintain because
templates and frontend code do not need broad exceptions.

7
00:00:45.816 --> 00:00:55.733
A policy should reflect the real asset model of the application, including
templates, bundled frontend assets, APIs, analytics, fonts, images, and
partner services.

8
00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:59.784
Report-only rollout is a practical way to learn before enforcement.

9
00:00:59.784 --> 00:01:05.231
In report-only mode, browsers can report potential violations without
blocking behavior.

10
00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:12.704
That helps teams discover unexpected inline code, third-party
dependencies, development-only assets, or edge-case pages.

11
00:01:12.704 --> 00:01:19.200
Reports can be noisy and may contain sensitive context, so collection and
review should be handled carefully.

12
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.019
The goal is to improve the policy, not to gather endless telemetry without
action.

13
00:01:24.019 --> 00:01:28.768
CSP does not replace context-aware output encoding or safe template
rendering.

14
00:01:28.768 --> 00:01:33.866
If untrusted data is rendered into a dangerous context, the code should
still be fixed.

15
00:01:33.866 --> 00:01:39.174
CSP can reduce impact and provide signals, but relying on it alone creates
brittle safety.

16
00:01:39.174 --> 00:01:46.577
A strong Python application uses CSP to support safe templates, safe APIs,
response minimization, and frontend discipline.

17
00:01:46.577 --> 00:01:49.720
It is a seatbelt, not permission to drive carelessly.
